      {
        "text": "Emiliano Arellano was appointed chair of Lynwood's Public Safety, Parking & Traffic Commission in 2025. He earned degrees in public administration and interdisciplinary studies from Cal State Dominguez Hills, and studied at Southwestern Law School. His campaign says he will focus on strengthening public safety, protecting immigrant families, expanding access to city resources, and making City Hall more responsive and transparent. His campaign states that his work on the commission helped get potholes filled.",
